  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday through next Friday)\nIssued at 1030 PM CDT Thu Jun 18 2026\n\nA shortwave will develop over the Plains late Saturday, eventually\npushing through Middle TN Sunday into Monday. This will bring the\nreturn of high humidity with high rain and storm chances, \nespecially Sunday night through Monday. A few strong storms with \ngusty winds may occur, but no widespread or organized severe \nstorms are expected.\n\nBeyond this system, the upper air pattern through next week favors\ncontinued on and off rain/storm chances as a broad trough over the\neastern states brings a series of weak disturbances. Showers and\nstorms will be mainly diurnal with a seasonably warm and humid\npattern. Lows will be mostly in the 60s and highs mainly in the \n80s.",
